The comments starting with "@@@" are placeholders for additional assertions that you can add based on the properties you want to verify about your code. You will just replace the "//" with your assertions. An example would be the following:

```cs
Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == Old_arrListContainsX);
``` 

This assertion asserts that the new array now contains the same elements as the old array. So, replace "//" with your assertions like that.

Remember that "Debug.Assert" checks a condition and, if the condition is false, the framework automatically throws an exception. So, be careful not to write assertions that would be slow or could crash your application (like unreachable code, infinite loops, etc.).--------------------Here are the corresponding Debug.Assert statements for the comments that start with "@@@":

```cs
Assert.LessOrEqual(New_arrListLastIndexOf_x, Old_arrListCount);
```

