Put this code where you want to assert that some specific behavior has occurred, after the tested code has been executed. This will make the testing process stop immediately, and indicate that the tested function or method has a bug that, according to the code, it should not produce.

```cs
[PexMethod]
public void PUT_AddContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
{
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int New_Ret = arrList.Add(x);
    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;

    System.Diagnostics.Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount > Old_arrListCount);

    // The rest of your current PUT_AddContract method...
}
```

